  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;is a weak field ligand.&nbsp;Crystal field stabilisation&nbsp;energy is maximum for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>8</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;cases with weak field ligands among the 3d-series elements.But&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CFSE</mi></math>&nbsp;increases from 3d to 5d series elements due to the increase in nuclear charge. Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>Os</mi><msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;complex case, the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CFSE</mi></math> is maximum.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
